SOAPBOX: I spent four days working hard to get a working setup ready, but
SOAPBOX: the computer had other ideas right before I planned to rest in
SOAPBOX: the afternoon prior to the contest... When I went to check that
SOAPBOX: everything was fine?since it had all worked perfectly the day
SOAPBOX: before?I found COM port errors the moment I fired up N1MM. I
SOAPBOX: checked the time no rest, but nothing critical yet. Then the
SOAPBOX: frustration set in?it was 2:10 AM local time. It was working, but
SOAPBOX: in AFSK mode?a nightmare for my ears... After a night's sleep, I
SOAPBOX: uninstalled the ports, wiped everything clean, and started the
SOAPBOX: installation over it was 8:30 AM, and I was finally ready by
SOAPBOX: noon?what a hassle... Still, I had a great time with my simple
SOAPBOX: wire antennas?no massive setup here: just an 80/40/20m fan dipole
SOAPBOX: and a homemade DX Commander. IC-7610 running 500W. Hopefully,
SOAPBOX: next year I?ll finally be able to put up a tower and proper
SOAPBOX: antennas! Thanks for the QSOs. 73 and good luck.
